---
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import PostHog from '../components/posthog.astro';
import '../styles/design-system.css';
const pilot = 'mailto:ben@keystonemere.com?subject=Aether%20Environmental%20Canvas%20Pilot';
const stages = [
 {n:'01',title:'Environmental inputs',body:'Scene settings, scheduled cues and configurable effect intensity.'},
 {n:'02',title:'State engine',body:'Translate supported inputs into scene-specific rendering parameters.'},
 {n:'03',title:'Aether Runtime',body:'Combine scene imagery, masks and browser-native visual effects.'},
 {n:'04',title:'Display output',body:'Render the environment locally using the selected device settings.'}
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="Explore Aether's browser-native environmental rendering, state engine and signage pilot architecture."/><title>Technology | Aether</title><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg"/><PostHog /></head>
<body><SiteHeader/><main id="main">
<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">The Aether Runtime</p><h1>Dynamic environments.<br/>Lightweight delivery.</h1><p class="lead">A browser-native environmental engine that separates visual content from the atmosphere that brings it to life.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/environmental-canvas/">Explore Environmental Canvas</a><a class="button" href={pilot}>Discuss a pilot</a></div></div><div class="panel hero-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Rendering model</p><div class="layer">Scene imagery &amp; spatial masks</div><div class="connector">+</div><div class="layer">Environmental state &amp; visual effects</div><div class="connector">↓</div><div class="layer output">Live environmental canvas</div><p class="small">Conceptual architecture. Effects vary by scene.</p></div></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">From state to screen</p><h2>One runtime. Configurable environments.</h2><p>Instead of replacing a video file to change the atmosphere, Aether can adjust supported visual parameters independently of the underlying scene.</p><div class="grid four">{stages.map(s=><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">{s.n}</p><h3>{s.title}</h3><p>{s.body}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">Environmental state</p><h2>Control the atmosphere.</h2><div class="grid three"><article class="panel"><h3>Weather</h3><p>Adjust supported rainfall, water ripples and vapour using scene-specific controls.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Motion</h3><p>Tune effect intensity to the visual requirements of a venue and its display hardware.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Time</h3><p>Use scheduled environmental states to vary the atmosphere throughout the day.</p></article></div><a class="link" href="/scene-lab/ullswater/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the Ullswater demonstration (new tab) →</a></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">Deployment architecture</p><h2>Render where the experience happens.</h2><div class="grid two"><article class="panel"><h3>Browser-native delivery</h3><p>Scene imagery and visual effects are combined on the display device. Playback does not require a continuous video stream. Initial asset delivery and future updates may require connectivity.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Hardware-conscious design</h3><p>Rendering profiles support tuning for different device capabilities. Raspberry Pi hardware is being used for pilot validation; supported configurations will be agreed per installation.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Playback monitoring</h3><p>The pilot player includes render progress monitoring and recovery logic. Long-duration stability and recovery behaviour remain under evaluation.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Deployment economics</h3><p>Local rendering is designed to limit streaming dependencies. Hardware, energy use, content delivery and support costs must be assessed for each deployment.</p></article></div></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">Development status</p><h2>Working technology. Measured validation.</h2><div class="grid three"><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">Implemented in prototypes</p><h3>Core runtime</h3><p>Scene effects, parameter controls, scheduled states and pilot player render monitoring.</p></article><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">Under validation</p><h3>Commercial reliability</h3><p>Hardware performance, long-duration playback, recovery and installation-specific requirements.</p></article><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">Planned direction</p><h3>Fleet management &amp; integrations</h3><p>Remote device administration, managed updates and commercial SDK access are not generally available.</p></article></div><p class="small">No certified hardware compatibility, guaranteed frame rate, energy saving or service-level commitment is implied.</p></section>
<section class="panel integration"><p class="eyebrow">Future integration opportunities</p><h2>An environmental layer for other platforms.</h2><p>Aether's planned integration direction includes embeddable environments and licensed runtime access for web platforms. Existing browser-based tools provide a foundation for exploring these opportunities. Commercial API and SDK specifications, licensing and support terms are yet to be defined.</p><a class="link" href="/tools/">Explore existing Aether tools →</a></section>
<section class="panel cta"><p class="eyebrow">Technical pilot enquiries</p><h2>Evaluate Aether in your environment.</h2><p>Discuss display specifications, playback requirements and measurable pilot success criteria.</p><a class="button primary" href={pilot}>Request a pilot</a></section>
</main><SiteFooter/></body></html>
<style>
:global(html){background:#070b12;color:#f4f7ff;font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif}
:global(body){margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 85% 5%,#172742 0%,transparent 38rem),#070b12;color:#f4f7ff}
main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:58px 22px 80px}section{padding:42px 0;border-top:1px solid #243248}section.hero{border:0;padding:20px 0 56px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center}h1,h2,h3{letter-spacing:-.045em;line-height:1.1}h1{font-size:clamp(42px,5.4vw,72px);margin:16px 0}h2{font-size:clamp(29px,3.5vw,44px);margin:12px 0 20px}h3{font-size:22px;margin:8px 0 12px}p{line-height:1.7;color:#b8c7dc;max-width:780px}.lead{font-size:clamp(17px,2vw,21px)}.eyebrow{color:#7dd3fc;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase}.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-top:28px}.button{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #40536d;border-radius:999px;padding:13px 19px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;font-size:14px}.primary{background:#d9f5ed;color:#092019;border-color:#d9f5ed}.grid{display:grid;gap:16px;margin:24px 0}.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr))}.three{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.two{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.panel{background:#101b2c;border:1px solid #30455d;border-radius:16px;padding:25px;min-width:0}.panel p{font-size:15px}.panel .eyebrow{font-size:11px}.hero-panel{background:linear-gradient(145deg,#101b2c,#142b32);padding:30px}.layer{border:1px solid #40536d;background:#0b1422;border-radius:10px;padding:20px;text-align:center;font-weight:700}.output{border-color:#6da99a;color:#d9f5ed}.connector{text-align:center;color:#7dd3fc;padding:9px}.small,.panel .small{font-size:12px;color:#a8b9cf}.link{color:#7dd3fc;font-size:14px;font-weight:600}.integration,.cta{margin-top:28px;padding:36px}.cta{text-align:center}.cta p{margin:12px auto 22px}a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #7dd3fc;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:900px){.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}section.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:28px 16px 55px}.four,.three,.two{grid-template-columns:1fr}section{padding:30px 0}.panel,.integration,.cta{padding:22px}}
</style>
